# BAS negation narrowing: when [int? x] fails, the type checker narrows x to
# Type::Negation(Int) in the false branch via apply_negation_narrowings.
# This exercises the BAS false-branch narrowing path added in the bas-core sprint.
[safe-inc: [fn [let x] [if [int? x] [+ x 1] 0]]
 r1: [safe-inc 5]
 r2: [safe-inc "hello"]]
=== out
["safe-inc": [fn [let x] ...]  "r1": 0  "r2": 0]
